Z||000019||Greg Piet||06-24-2001||02:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroPerformance:<BR><B>Just saw it again. Anyone who thought this movie was dumb either:<P>1. Does not like cars<BR>2. Does not like racing cars<BR>3. Prefers tamer movies such as "Stepmom"<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>For the little list above<BR>I do like cars(way more than what is considered healthy)!  <BR>I have never seen "stepmom"!<BR>I do like racing cars(way more than what is considered healthy again)!<P>I have not seen it just yet, but I am pretty sure I will be in the same opinion as 88Formula.<BR>I saw a clip on Leno, where two cars were "racing" at some speed above a buck forty on what appeared to be city streets.<BR>One of the cars had its diamond plate floorboard rattle loose(likely due to its fart can resonating everything loose) and then fly off after it fell under the car.<BR>For those of you that <B>actually</B> race you know as well as I that if something like that happened it would cut a tire to be consistent with Murphys laws of racing.<BR>Also in this clip there was one car with two "go fast" buttons on the steering wheel, and the other car had a "go fast" button on the center console (about where the AC blower switch is on out Fieros).  The few times I have gone 140 the LAST thing I want to do is take my hand off the wheel and go fiddle with the radio, or press a "go fast" button so there is a surge of power when I only have one hand on the wheel. <P>And as far as that "fly" wing that is "tight" (I dont know which one your referring to), go check out a Civic message board as I am sure they have a section devoted entirely to wings.  I will stop thinking ill of multi tiered wings that are 3 feet off the car when professional racing cars use them.  When was the last time you saw a dual wing on an indy car going 230mph? <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 SM<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">    <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fiero5||06-24-2001||03:21 PM||||For those of you who expect movies to follow reality and the laws of physics at all times, don't hold your breath! Movie makers think that to make a movie extra entertaining they need to stretch things and overlook some to make the story work.<BR>How many action movies have you seen where there were not any mistakes that made you roll your eyes a bit in a scene or two.<BR>Rambo was awesome, but when five guys are shooting machine guns at a guy 20 feet away running in a straight line and not one bullet hits him? Did you know that in outer space there is no air for sound? Yet in every sci-movie I can remember, they have sound effects in space. Even in the movie Alien, they billed it as "In space, no one can hear you scream". Meaning that there is no sound in space, yet they had rocket engine sounds, and explosions, etc. It would be boring to watch a sci-movie with no outer space sounds.<BR>I could go on with tons of movies, but you all know what I mean.<BR>Go to the movie, enjoy it and hope that one day soon someone will make something like this with a Fiero or two, or three, or four, etc in it.<P>In fact I am doing a Fiero I-Movie right now.<P>Steve<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000021||Black88GT||06-24-2001||04:46 PM||||I saw it last night, it was OK.  Not nearly as good as Gone in 60 Seconds.  The ricer exhausts were pretty loud and annoying.<P>At the theater I counted 13 Blue Civic Si's and 9 Black ones, countless other Civic hatchbacks and fake Integra type R's.  It was like a ricer convention.||||reg||1
Z||000022||dr fritz||06-24-2001||05:07 PM||||Here is my 0.02 cents worth.  I greatly enjoyed the movie... if you want facts go watch a documentry, if you want fun see the movie!!!  yes it had no plot, yes the acting was average at best, and yes there were too many rice rockets... but... we already new that before we went to see the movie right?  the entertainment factor in this movie is all in the car scenes, races and chases... this is what you are spending youre money on... and i thought it was well worth it, in fact i plan on seeing it again!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||OverDrive||06-24-2001||05:11 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> LMAO Thats exactly how it was here, I went and saw swordfish on the day Fast and the furious came out. Man it was RICE CITY! like civics, EVERYWHERE! I was actually scared someone was going to sneak up on me and put a "Powered by Honda" sticker on me when I wasn't looking!<BR>Some guy had a banner on his car that said "The Fast and The Furious" I just walked away shaking my head feeling a lot more dumber than before I had came.||||reg||1
Z||000024||MikeSchaefer||06-24-2001||06:42 PM||||A Riceboy fairytale  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>ok, now let me get this straight; the Ferrari gets beat by the ricer.....  the Ferrari gets beat by the ricer!!!  I don't think so!!!!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000025||mrgone||06-24-2001||07:16 PM||||i have a real player video of a ferrari getting beat by what looks like a dx hatchback at a night race<P>||||reg||1
Z||000026||kslish||06-24-2001||07:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MikeSchaefer:<BR><B>A Riceboy fairytale   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>ok, now let me get this straight; the Ferrari gets beat by the ricer.....  the Ferrari gets beat by the ricer!!!  I don't think so!!!!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>While I don't want to defend this movie too much (I took it for what it was, fictional entertainment) the idea of a modified Twin Turbo Supra beating a Ferrari in a straight line isn't that far fetched.  Stock, a Ferrari 355 like in the movie has 380hp/268 lb.ft of torque and has a pretty peaky powerband.  A stock Supra Turbo puts out 320hp/315ft-lb and weighs about the same as the Ferrari.  Turn up the boost on the Supra and make some other mods, you can easily have around 400hp. <P>Ferrari's have never been exceptional straight line cars.  They are more known for their handling and their position as a "status symbol"  My local mechanic has a fly yellow 308 and it sucks in all out straight line acceleration (but it sounds cool all wound up).  <P>Of course, if the movie had went way outside the bounds of reality (like a Civic beating the Ferrari) I probably would have been kicked out of the theater for laughing so hard.<P>I'll take one of those Nissan Skyline GT-R's that were in the movie though.  I think it would be a good daily driver   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Formula||06-24-2001||07:32 PM||||Im pretty sure a supra like that would beat a ferrari||||reg||1
Z||000028||Bazooka||06-24-2001||07:49 PM||||    Went to Great Lakes Dragaway(Illinois) a few weeks back for just 'Time Runs'. There were supercharged and turboed Hondas, MR-2's, and all kinds of RiceBurners. They were all turning low 15's with their cars and I coudn't avoid having to race 4 or 5 of them myself. Of course they are no match for a V8 Fiero like mine.<BR>****************************************<BR>[QUOTE]Originally posted by kslish:<BR>[B] While I don't want to defend this movie too much (I took it for what it was, fictional entertainment) the idea of a modified Twin Turbo Supra beating a Ferrari in a straight line isn't that far fetched.  Stock, a Ferrari 355 like in the movie has 380hp/268 lb.ft of torque and has a pretty peaky powerband.  A stock Supra Turbo puts out 320hp/315ft-lb and weighs about the same as the Ferrari.  Turn up the boost on the Supra and make some other mods, you can easily have around 400hp. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||AkursedX||06-24-2001||10:42 PM||||Just got back from the show.  It was a pretty good movie.  It had alot of little errors in it that got really annoying.  Like the NOS in the middle of the race.  Racing w/ full interiors and enormous stereos.  But that was expected, but overall, i liked it.<P>And on a sidenote.....I killed a riced out 1st gen. Talon that followed me out of the lot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000030||FieroPerformance||06-24-2001||11:59 PM||||I've seen the movie 3 times so far. Sure it isn't exactly believable but that isn't the point of a movie. Movies are for entertainment only, not education. Fast and the Furious is loosly based on street racing, the rest is hollywood. I would not consider the cars in this movie "rice" by any means. My personal definition of a ricer is someone who puts money into their car to make it look fast without actually upgrading the performance. The cars in this movie had everything and could back up the radical appearances. But hey, you have your opinions and I have mine. No movie I have ever seen gets me as pumped up about driving as this one does though.<P><BR>-Charlie<BR>----<BR>jackalrr@hotmail.com<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000031||Smoooooth GT||06-25-2001||09:48 AM||||I saw it with my lil' girl lastnight....  I see now that I need some NOS to go along with my T-3....  lol   Steve<P>------------------<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_sig_3.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000032||1FST2M6||06-25-2001||09:49 AM||||their continunity directors need a little work.. as they are talking about the "turbo eclipse" and he pops the hood..  you'll see it's naturaly aspirated and there is a brospeed header where the stock 2.0 manifold should be.. on a DSM the turbo is VERY obvious and the lighting in the shot was directly on the manifold.. and when Dom hit his "sneaky pete" system and they follow the course of the nitrous.. once the fog gets to the comustion chamber what does it encounter? a piston..  uum everyone knows the RX7 is a rotary...  sorry.. but i went with the guys from the shop, 10 people from miata.net and 9 people from teamfocaljet.com (focus) (28 of us!) we all had a good time watching the not so bright kids get pulled over right and left trying to be cool leaving the parking lot after the movie... it really reminded us too of "Point break" with a similar plot line... the supra is for sale on e-bay for $75k what a deal!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> entertaining, surley worth the $7.50.... but i won't buy the movie.  <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
